  "id": "social-identity-theory",
  "term": "social identity theory",
  "definition": "Social identity theory is a social psychology framework for understanding how shared social norms and group meanings become part of people’s sense of identity and reputation. In this source, it is used to explain how wider expectations can shape family rules, responses, and relationships.",
